course: dictionary
lesson: 14484
title: Pathogens: tiny causes of disease
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pathogen is a tiny living thing that can cause disease. Bacteria, viruses and fungi can all be pathogens, and they are too small to see without a microscope.
explain: Not every germ is a pathogen, but some are harmful. When a pathogen gets into your body, it can make you ill. «The cut let harmful pathogens into her body, and she felt poorly.»
explain: Pathogens spread from person to person, and through dirty hands and food. Your immune system fights them, and simple habits help too. «Washing your hands with soap helps kill pathogens.»
fact: A pathogen is a tiny living thing, such as a bacterium, virus or fungus, that can cause disease.
fact: «Harmful pathogens» are the kind that make people ill.
fact: «Kill pathogens» means destroy them so they can no longer cause disease.
fact: Soap, cooking food properly and vaccines all help protect us from pathogens.
fact: The immune system is the body's defence against pathogens.
exercise: «Harmful pathogens can make you ill.» What is a pathogen? | A kind of food that goes bad quickly | A medicine you swallow with water | A large animal that lives on a farm | *A tiny living thing that can cause disease
exercise: «Washing your hands with soap helps kill pathogens.» What does the sentence say soap does to pathogens? | *Destroys them so they cannot make you ill | Makes them bigger | Hides them under your nails | Feeds them
exercise: Which of these can be a pathogen? | *A virus that causes a cold | A rainbow | A chair | A cloud
test: Which of these is a pathogen? | A glass of water | *A fungus that can cause an infection | A rock on the beach | A pencil case
test: «Vaccines help the immune system fight pathogens before they make you ill.» What does the immune system do? | Makes food taste better | Keeps you warm in winter | Helps you grow taller | *Fights off pathogens
exam: Why do we wash our hands before we eat? | *To remove pathogens that could make us ill | To stop our hands getting dry | To make the soap smell nice | To make our hands warmer
